  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — specifically, the skewness of the lotteries — is not considered by the individual. The individual does not mention the 1% chance of 0 Euros or any unfavorable outcome, nor does the individual refer to the distribution of probabilities in terms of skewness. Instead, the individual focuses on the possibility of a higher gain (up to 100 Euros more) and the near-certainty of a positive outcome, which reflects a focus on expected value or risk of loss, not skewness. The decision reason requires recognizing that A has a greater portion of probability on unfavorable outcomes (0 Euros), making it more right-skewed, and thus preferring A. Since the individual does not consider this aspect of the distribution, nor justify the choice based on skewness, the decision reason was not used. Therefore, the individual did not apply the skewness-based reason to the decision-making process.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
